  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).",
    "In a large Dutch oven, combine the beef short ribs, coconut milk, tamarind paste, fish sauce, brown sugar, crushed black pepper, rice vinegar, and palm sugar. Cover the pot with a lid and transfer it to the preheated oven.",
    "Roast for 2 hours, or until the beef is tender and falling off the bone.",
    "While the beef is roasting, prepare the roasted vegetables: slice the eggplant, carrots, and bell peppers into bite-sized pieces, and toss them with a tablespoon of oil and a sprinkle of salt on a baking sheet. Roast in the oven for 20-25 minutes, or until tender and lightly caramelized.",
    "Add the roasted vegetables, fresh cilantro, and fresh mint to the pot with the beef. Stir to combine and let simmer for 10-15 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld together.",
    "Serve the larb over steamed jasmine rice, garnished with crushed peanuts, lime wedges, and additional Thai basil if desired.",
